import Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic
import Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum

/-!
# C1 — the `k = 54` certificate's two forms and the inequality

`Iint = Σ_{i,j} c_i·c_j·WI(k_i + k_j)` over the coefficients and
`Jint = Σ_{x,y} W_x·W_y·WJ(k_x + k_y)` over the collected marginal, each the sum of its symmetric
half's row blocks (`Ihalf`, `Jhalf`), each block's value certified by `decide +kernel`. With
`I = Iint/100!` and `J = Jint/((24!)²·101!)`, `cert54` is `54·J/I > 4.0015`:
`0 < Iint ∧ 40015·Iint·(24!)²·101! < 10000·54·Jint·100!`.

The blocks are cut by pair count (the kernel's memory grows with the pairs one declaration
evaluates); `scripts/c1/lean_cert54.py` writes this file. Nothing here bears on twin primes.
-/

set_option maxRecDepth 1000000
set_option linter.style.longLine false
-- One theorem at a time, and nothing of a checked theorem kept: with asynchronous elaboration each
-- theorem's snapshot is retained to the end of the file, and a file of these theorems grows to
-- ~15 GB (measured); synchronously the file's peak is its largest theorem's (~3 GB).
set_option Elab.async false

namespace SaltC1.Cert54

